        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/259692397?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Marks <code class=\"notranslate\">Element.part</code> as read-only in the <code class=\"notranslate\">Element</code> interface property list, matching the dedicated <code class=\"notranslate\">Element.part</code> documentation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45860.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5600928406\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45860\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45860/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45860\">#45860</a>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The dedicated <code class=\"notranslate\">Element.part</code> page describes the property as read-only, but the <code class=\"notranslate\">Element</code> interface overview was missing the read-only indicator. This change makes the overview consistent with the property documentation.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is a documentation-only change.</p>",
