        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89024979?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add the <code class=\"notranslate\">{{ReadOnlyInline}}</code> label to <code class=\"notranslate\">Element.part</code> on the Element interface page, matching sibling read-only properties such as <code class=\"notranslate\">Element.classList</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Element.children</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Element.part</code> is a read-only property (like <code class=\"notranslate\">classList</code>, it exposes a <code class=\"notranslate\">DOMTokenList</code>). The listing on the Element page was missing the read-only badge.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45860.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5600928406\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45860\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45860/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45860\">#45860</a></p>",
