        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/236759479?u=6a2b51441b1015f9a4beae865bfcb3f1a2ea9899&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The Values section listed the one-, two- and three-value combinations of <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;number&gt;</code> and explained <code class=\"notranslate\">auto</code> in a paragraph below them. This lists <code class=\"notranslate\">auto</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;integer&gt;</code> as the two entries, with the position rules (and what an omitted second or third value becomes) under <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;integer&gt;</code>, as suggested in the review of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4992022479\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44937\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/44937/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44937\">#44937</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It also changes <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;number&gt;</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;integer&gt;</code>: the spec grammar is <code class=\"notranslate\">[ auto | &lt;integer [0,∞]&gt; ]{1,3}</code>, and non-integers are rejected.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">auto</code> was the only value not in the definition list, and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;number&gt;</code> suggested that values like <code class=\"notranslate\">1.5</code> are allowed.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Spec: <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-4/#propdef-hyphenate-limit-chars\" rel=\"nofollow\">CSS Text 4, <code class=\"notranslate\">hyphenate-limit-chars</code></a> (\"If the third value is missing, it is the same as the second. If the second value is missing, then it is auto.\")</li>\n<li>WPT <a href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-text/parsing/hyphenate-limit-chars-invalid.html\"><code class=\"notranslate\">hyphenate-limit-chars-invalid.html</code></a> treats <code class=\"notranslate\">1.2</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">1 1.2</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">1 2 1.2</code> as invalid.</li>\n<li>Checked in headless Edge 153 with <code class=\"notranslate\">CSS.supports(\"hyphenate-limit-chars\", …)</code>: <code class=\"notranslate\">10</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10 4</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10 4 4</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">auto 3</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10 auto 4</code> are true; <code class=\"notranslate\">1.2</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10.0</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10 4.5</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10 4 4.5</code> are false.</li>\n<li>markdownlint-cli2, prettier and cspell pass on the file.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45071.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5112357853\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45071\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45071/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45071\">#45071</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45854",
            "title": "hyphenate-limit-chars: list auto and <integer> as separate values",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-26T09:27:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-26T09:24:43.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "RizgarOzan",
                "url": "https://github.com/RizgarOzan"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Turns out that there's simply no way to tell if a PWA is running as an installed app.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #34928.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2419254063\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/34928\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/34928/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/34928\">#34928</a>.</p>",
