        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96150?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've added a one-line note that, on Windows, <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: cursive</code> means Comic Sans MS.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It's an unfortunate quirk of the web that Chrome, Edge, Firefox, and Opera all render <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: cursive</code> using Comic Sans MS on Windows.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">MDN indicates that <code class=\"notranslate\">cursive</code> implies that the glyphs would be at least partially connected by joining strokes, but Comic Sans MS doesn't connect any of its glyphs. IMO, Comic Sans MS is not \"cursive,\" at all.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I was caught very much by surprise when I used <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: cursive</code> and tested on iOS, Android, and macOS, and got Apple Chancery on iOS/macOS and Dancing Script on Android, but got Comic Sans MS on all browsers on Windows. (Comic Sans MS has a casual, comedic vibe. It was very much <em>not</em> what I was going for when I selected <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: cursive</code>.)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If a note like this had appeared on MDN, it would have saved me some embarrassment.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45851",
            "title": "Document that `font-family: cursive` is Comic Sans MS on Windows",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-25T21:41:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-25T21:28:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dfabulich",
                "url": "https://github.com/dfabulich"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">@supports</code> was missing from the first example.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45849",
            "title": "Add @supports to column-height property",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-25T13:48:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-25T13:07:34.000Z",
